# Card Data Handling

## Loading Set Data

Use the centralized loader:

```typescript
import { loadSetData, availableSets } from './data/sets/index'

// Load set data
const data = await loadSetData(setCode, language)
const cards = data.cards  // Array of CardData
```

## CardData Interface

Key fields from LorcanaJSON:

```typescript
interface CardData {
  id: number           // Unique ID (consistent across languages)
  name: string         // Card name
  fullName: string     // "Name - Version"
  cost: number         // Ink cost
  color: string        // Amber, Amethyst, Emerald, Ruby, Sapphire, Steel
  rarity: string       // Common, Uncommon, Rare, Super Rare, Legendary, Enchanted
  type: string         // Character, Item, Action, Song, Location
  
  // Character only
  strength?: number
  willpower?: number
  lore?: number
  
  inkwell: boolean     // Can be inked
  fullText?: string    // Card text
  images: { full: string }
}
```

## Rarity Localization

Rarity names vary by language. Use the `rarityMapping`:

```typescript
const rarityMapping: Record<string, Record<string, string>> = {
  en: { Common: 'Common', Uncommon: 'Uncommon', ... },
  de: { Common: 'Gewöhnlich', Uncommon: 'Ungewöhnlich', ... },
  // ...
}

const localizedRarity = rarityMapping[language][englishRarity]
```

## Location Cards

Detect by type (varies by language):

```typescript
const locationTypes = ['Location', 'Ort', 'Lieu', 'Luogo']
const isLocation = locationTypes.includes(card.type)
```
